  "coordinate_transform": "The source uses the P21nm subgroup origin and prints Fe=(0,0.25,0), H=(0.5,0.25,0), O1=(0.348,0.485,0), and O2=(0.651,0.015,0). Subtracting 0.25 from y places Fe on standard Pnnm 2a and H on 2d; source O1 and O2 then merge into one symmetry-equivalent 4g site represented by (0.348,0.235,0).",
  "notes": "The diffraction structure is the 50 GPa static Pnnm low-spin calculation of Insixiengmay and Stixrude (2023). It supplies a complete phase-specific positional model because Thompson et al. (2017) publish lattice metrics and bond geometry but not fractional atomic coordinates. The structure calculation uses a different exchange-correlation treatment and magnetic ordering from the Thompson volumetric EOS, so its 47.975 A^3 cell is retained as a diffraction reference rather than forced onto the EOS curve."
 },
 "notes": "This material is separate from e_feooh, whose reference structure is the hydrogen-off-center P21nm phase. The Pnnm site multiplicities give Fe2O4H2 (Z=2).",
